{
  "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
  "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert J. Wagner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On April 3rd of 1992, Judge Foster dismissed criminal charges against Timothy Hall. She noted on the docket, case removed from docket, defendant deceased, and then signed her name."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert J. Wagner (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAGNER: Well, the rule that's in place here, the rule from Holloway v. Arkansas, the rule from Cuyler v. Sullivan, the rule from Wood v. Georgia, is an appropriate rule, and it's appropriate because it requires that the trial judge or the -- or the judge in the case knows or reasonably should know that there is, in fact, a particular conflict."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But I was asking you what the rule should be, not the rule -- I probably wasn't specific enough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: All right. So, if you're right then on this point, then there was loads of prejudice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court, in fact, found no prejudice, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wagner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAGNER: I don't believe that you necessarily show one by showing the other. In an actual conflict situation, it's really the potential of a lapse in representation that the Court focuses on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But if, on the facts of that case, those two are opposite sides of the same coin -- there's no -- if you show one, then you inevitably show the other -- then how can we extract the words of the decision from the fact background against which Justice Powell was writing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Are you -- are you arguing that we should adopt that rule? I mean, if we did, that would -- that would answer the point that has just been raised."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wagner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAGNER: We are not, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court: The Fourth Circuit correctly required a showing of adverse effect for Mickens to establish a conflict of interest claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Harris",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HARRIS: Holloway is -- is not been overruled. It is perfectly good law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: May I ask you this question? Do you think the lawyer in this case had a duty to tell his client that he had represented the victim? Just an ethical -- not a constitutional duty, as an ethical matter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: The trouble I'm having with the standard is not whether the judge happens to know he should have looked in or shouldn't have looked into it, which were unusual circumstances. If a lawyer is under a real conflict -- a real one, a very serious one, a terrible one -- his client cannot get effective assistance. So, I would have thought that's the standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States, as amicus curiae",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: I would say that Holloway is a special case where prejudice was presumed conclusively based on two factors. The first is that deference to the contemporaneous judgment of counsel that he was operating under a disabling conflict, and when he's representing that he's operating under a disabling conflict, it's not just a representation that he has a conflict, but that this is going to affect his performance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Suppose the victim were the fiance of the lawyer's niece and the lawyer was very close to the niece, and he says, I can't do this, judge. I -- I can't represent this murderer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: Well, then you have a Holloway situation if the -- if the defendant -- defense counsel is representing that he's operating under a disabling conflict and the judge doesn't conduct an inquiry, then there's automatic reversal at that point. That's the Holloway carve-out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Of course, the irony of the rule is that it gives greater protection when the lawyer is -- conceals -- unethically conceals a known conflict than when he's candid with the court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gornstein",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: -- against the defendant on both of those points. The district court carefully examined the questions of whether there was a conflict and whether there was an adverse effect. Those were the correct inquiries."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-00-9285",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "db0ed2ead581f70e451b5c8d43e8231a26be5b199974a619282a03f3b6a073d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-db0ed2ead581-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Mr. Wagner. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
